    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35055" root="قبح" body-key="q">
    
      4 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اقبح</span></b>  <i>He did</i> [or <i>said</i>] <i>what was bad, evil,
abominable, foul,</i> or <i>unseemly.</i> (S, A, K.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2- 
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَا أَقْبَحَ وَجْهَهُ</span> is said in reviling a man [as meaning <i>How foul, unseemly, unsightly, ugly,</i> or <i>hideous,
is his face!</i>]. (Ham p. 138.)

